00:15:48,780 --> 00:15:53,500
and the power and might that ruled the rails for nearly two centuries before it.

191
00:15:56,040 --> 00:16:00,640
The development of the steam locomotive was both evolutionary and revolutionary.

192
00:16:01,500 --> 00:16:04,300
The biggest problem initially was finding the proportions,

193
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:10,400
the proportions between the boiler, the cylinders, the drivers, and the linkage mechanism.

194
00:16:10,401 --> 00:16:16,880
The first locomotive that really got it all right in the right proportions was a locomotive called the John Bull.

195
00:16:18,860 --> 00:16:26,000
Mechanics put the John Bull into commission in 1831, and it became the first locomotive ever to be duplicated.

196
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:36,120
But the wood-burning model was quickly outmoded as locomotives increased rapidly in size and power.

197
00:16:36,121 --> 00:16:43,120
Wood was used generally in American railroads until sometime right after the Civil War.

198
00:16:43,121 --> 00:16:47,120
And what happened was that a lot of territories that the railroads were going in,

199
00:16:47,121 --> 00:16:51,120
in the prairies and the plains, there weren't any trees around.

200
00:16:51,121 --> 00:16:55,120
Most locomotives introduced at the end of the 19th century burned coal.

201
00:16:55,121 --> 00:17:02,120
Back in those days, about every three, four years, you'd get a larger locomotive.

202
00:17:02,121 --> 00:17:07,120
locomotive. They just kept advancing the technology every couple of years and

203
00:17:07,121 --> 00:17:11,720
it's like your automobile. Somebody would come out with a new model and the

204
00:17:11,721 --> 00:17:15,440
railroads would try it out and find out that yeah this is pretty efficient and

205
00:17:15,441 --> 00:17:20,480
we'll buy some of these. Early 20th century locomotives easily dwarfed their

206
00:17:20,481 --> 00:17:26,000
predecessors. Their size and power may have changed drastically.

207
00:17:26,001 --> 00:17:31,000
However there were few fundamental changes in how they worked.

208
00:17:31,001 --> 00:17:36,000
Pressurized steam enters one side of the cylinder and pushes the piston away.

209
00:17:36,001 --> 00:17:42,000
A valve shifts the steam to the other side and forces the piston back.

210
00:17:42,001 --> 00:17:49,000
A series of connected rods convert the piston's back-and-forth motion to the rotational motion of the wheels.

211
00:17:49,001 --> 00:17:56,000
By the Second World War, the steam locomotive had reached its pinnacle of technological development.

212
00:17:56,001 --> 00:18:01,000
They were a source of pride for the men who had a chance to work on them.

